														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">What is the difference between SEO, GEO, AEO, and LLMO?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-10214" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="14" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-10214"><p>SEO (Search Engine Optimization) is ranking in classic search results. AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) is structuring content so it can be extracted as a direct answer by features like AI Overviews, featured snippets, and voice assistants. GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) is engineering your brand and content to be selected and cited by generative AI engines when they synthesize an answer. LLMO (Large Language Model Optimization) is the broader discipline of shaping how LLMs perceive your brand entity across their training data and live retrieval. Digiexe treats all four as one unified strategy because the underlying signals — entity clarity, authoritative citations, structured data, and unique information gain — overlap heavily.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
