														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">How do you get a brand cited by ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Google AI Overviews?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-10215" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="15" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-10215"><p>Six things, in priority order: build a clean, machine-readable entity (consistent NAP, sameAs links, JSON-LD Organization schema, Wikidata or Wikipedia presence where eligible); publish content with information gain — original data, expert quotes, first-hand experience — that LLMs cannot find elsewhere; format pages as self-contained answer blocks with a direct one-sentence answer in the first 50 words of each H2 or H3; earn citations from sources LLMs already trust (Reddit, YouTube, G2, Clutch, industry publications, Wikipedia-tier outlets); implement FAQ, HowTo, Article, Product, and Review schema; and monitor and benchmark share of model monthly using tools like Profound, Peec AI, or our internal Digiexe AI visibility tracker.</p></div>
				</div>
